WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:01.274
(light whimsical music)

00:00:01.274 --> 00:00:03.318
- [Narrator] The Ultra 6633 is

00:00:03.318 --> 00:00:04.985
a 352 mile-long race

00:00:07.045 --> 00:00:08.545
across the Arctic.

00:00:09.712 --> 00:00:11.085
It's cold.

00:00:11.085 --> 00:00:14.231
- [Racer] It didn't
really get above minus 45.

00:00:14.231 --> 00:00:15.833
- [Narrator] It's long.

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:19.363
- [Racer] I think that took me 150 hours.

00:00:19.363 --> 00:00:22.448
- [Narrator] And most
people, don't finish it.

00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:24.115
- [Racer] It's cold!

00:00:26.694 --> 00:00:28.296
- [Narrator] This is Dave Berridge.

00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:29.698
He lives on the Isle of Wight.

00:00:29.698 --> 00:00:32.766
- [Dave] It's a small island
off the south coast of England.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:36.933
- [Narrator] And last year,
he won the Ultra 6633.

00:00:38.014 --> 00:00:40.923
So, I'm talking to him
about what it feels like

00:00:40.923 --> 00:00:43.925
to race across the Arctic.
- Come back.

00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:47.813
A typical marathon is 26.2 miles long.

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:51.824
So, this is like 14 of them, back-to-back.

00:00:51.824 --> 00:00:52.889
(somber piano music)

00:00:52.889 --> 00:00:55.115
The distance is isolating.

00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:57.066
- [Dave] You're on your
own for like two days

00:00:57.066 --> 00:00:57.899
at a time.

00:00:58.819 --> 00:01:02.041
- [Narrator] And with negative
45 degree temperatures,

00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:03.791
it feels even longer.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.550
- [Dave] Everything out there is big.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.290
There's just nothing to gage distance by.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.342
There's nothing to judge anything by.

00:01:12.342 --> 00:01:15.201
You can see nothing but white.

00:01:15.201 --> 00:01:17.151
So, you start to think, on less sleep,

00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:18.800
am I dreaming this?

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.437
Am I actually moving?

00:01:20.437 --> 00:01:23.095
It's like being in a painting.

00:01:23.095 --> 00:01:26.497
- [Narrator] It took Dave
six days to finish the race,

00:01:26.497 --> 00:01:29.664
and he only slept a total of 10 hours.

00:01:30.793 --> 00:01:32.952
"It's that exhaustion," he says,

00:01:32.952 --> 00:01:35.582
"that causes you to lose your mind."

00:01:35.582 --> 00:01:36.945
(light eerie music)

00:01:36.945 --> 00:01:40.116
- [Dave] Your mind just
starts imagining all sorts.

00:01:40.116 --> 00:01:42.972
I've went through an avenue of trees

00:01:42.972 --> 00:01:45.363
and I thought I was going
through a disco party,

00:01:45.363 --> 00:01:48.363
and every time I approached somebody,

00:01:48.363 --> 00:01:51.215
they stopped talking
and just looked at me.

00:01:51.215 --> 00:01:53.479
- [Narrator] But, you can't stop.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:54.744
- [Dave] You've got to keep moving.

00:01:54.744 --> 00:01:58.133
You think, "What on earth
is that coming towards me?"

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.818
And, you know, within two
minutes you're shivering.

00:02:00.818 --> 00:02:03.115
You shouldn't have stopped
to look at something

00:02:03.115 --> 00:02:04.915
that's not there.

00:02:04.915 --> 00:02:07.306
(light pulsating music)

00:02:07.306 --> 00:02:08.978
I achieved what I wanted to achieve,

00:02:08.978 --> 00:02:11.184
and I finished it, and I'm very grateful

00:02:11.184 --> 00:02:13.576
and very lucky to have finished it.

00:02:13.576 --> 00:02:15.155
Out of all the races I've done,

00:02:15.155 --> 00:02:18.870
it's one of the most mentally
challenging races out there,

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:22.399
and it's probably the race
that commands the most respect.

00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:24.280
Anybody who finishes that will...

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.177
Well, I would say,
they've got my admiration.

00:02:27.177 --> 00:02:30.094
(slow eerie music)

